      "id": "u72suez",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economic Planning"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic planning in India was initiated to achieve systematic growth, self-reliance, modernization, and social justice.",
        "The Planning Commission was established in 1950 to formulate Five-Year Plans for national development.",
        "NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission in 2015 to serve as an advisory think tank promoting cooperative federalism.",
        "Key functions of NITI Aayog focus on a bottom-up approach to development and strategic policy vision."
      ],
      "id": "uhyetz6"
    },
